# MNIST Digit Classification Using SVM

## Project Overview

This project uses a Support Vector Machine (SVM) with an RBF kernel to classify handwritten digits from the MNIST dataset.

## Dataset

* 60,000 training images
* 10,000 test images
* 784 pixel features per image
* Pixel values normalized to the range [0, 1]

## Model

* Algorithm: Support Vector Machine (SVM)
* Kernel: RBF
* Best parameters: C=10, gamma=scale

## Results

* Validation accuracy: 97.10%
* Test accuracy: 96.82%

## Files

* `mnist_svm.ipynb`: Notebook containing the code, training, evaluation, and results.

## Technologies

Python, NumPy, Pandas, Matplotlib, and scikit-learn.
